[Composer "Fernando Saavedra (after Georges Barbier)"]
[Source "Glasgow Weekly Citizen"]
[Year "1895"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/1KP5/3r4/8/8/8/k7 w - - 0 1"]

{ White's pawn is one step from queening, but the rook keeps checking – and has a stalemate trick ready. }
1. c7 Rd6+ 2. Kb5 Rd5+ 3. Kb4 Rd4+ 4. Kb3 Rd3+ 5. Kc2 Rd4
{ Black sets a trap: if White queens, Rc4+ forces stalemate. } 6. c8=R $1
{ A rook is enough, and it cannot be stalemated in this way. It threatens Ra8 mate. } ( 6. c8=Q $2
{ Rc4+ 7. Qxc4 is stalemate. } 6... Rc4+ 7. Qxc4 ) 6... Ra4 7. Kb3
{ The rook is attacked and Rc1 mate is threatened: White wins. } *

[Event "Réti Study"]
